00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:13,500
Goya's Ghosts is a drama, history film directed by Miloš Forman.

2
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Painter Francisco Goya becomes involved with the Spanish Inquisition
after his muse, Inés, is arrested by the church for heresy.

3
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:28,500
Her family turns to him, hoping that his connection with fanatical
Inquisitor Lorenzo, whom he is painting, can secure her release.

4
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Lorenzo Casamares, played by Javier Bardem.

5
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:43,500
Inés Bilbatúa / Alicia, played by Natalie Portman.

6
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Francisco Goya, played by Stellan Skarsgård.

7
00:49:52,500 --> 00:49:58,500
King Carlos IV, played by Randy Quaid.

8
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Tomás Bilbatúa, played by José Luis Gómez.

9
01:04:07,500 --> 01:04:13,500
Inquisitor General, played by Michael Lonsdale.

10
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Goya's Ghosts is a 2006 biographical drama film, directed by Miloš Forman (his final directorial
feature before his death in 2018), and written by him and Jean-Claude Carrière.

11
01:18:22,500 --> 01:18:28,500
The film stars Javier Bardem, Natalie Portman, and Stellan Skarsgård as
Francisco Goya, and was filmed on location in Spain during late 2005.

12
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film was written, produced, and performed in
English although it is a Spanish production.

13
01:32:37,500 --> 01:32:43,500
Although the historical setting of the film is authentic, the story about Goya trying to defend a
model is fictional, as are the characters Brother Lorenzo and the Bilbatúa family.

14
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
The film explores themes of rape, religion and
supernatural, heresy, napoleon bonaparte, loss.

15
01:46:52,500 --> 01:46:58,500
The tone is emotional.
